3c942-2f987 | 2026-06-29T12:14:54Z | session:3c942260-311d-4e00-8bcc-204045ea87b3 | - **High:** add explicit idempotent **`shutdown()`** (not just Drop; avoid `close` — Kotlin friction from #2149). [...] User: [Agent task result: Dynamic workflow "Implement + review the #2389 UniFFI app-lifecycle/byte-doorway scaffold (foundational)" completed] \n {"code":{"opened_pr":true,"pr_url":"https://github.com/pablof7z/nostr-multi-platform/pull/2397","branch":"ns-2389-uniffi-scaffold","summary":"New crate nmp-uniffi (#2389): UniFFI 0.29 proc-macro bindings wrapping nmp-native-runtime. Exposes NmpApp (Arc-wrapped), UpdateSink callback interface (quiescence-safe), and DispatchOutcome record. FFI-free dispatch core moved to nmp-native-runtime::action_dispatch returning typed DispatchOutcome; C-ABI and UniFFI both consume the same implementation. Fixed a NmpApp::shutdown() deadlock where actor_starter's captured update_tx kept the listener thread alive forever when the actor was never started. Generated Swift/Kotlin bindings checked in under crates/nmp-uniffi/generated/ with CI drift gate.","dispatch_core_moved":"Moved from crates/nmp-ffi/src/action/bytes.rs to crates/nmp-native-runtime/src/action_dispatch.rs as pub fn dispatch_action_bytes_typed(app: &NmpApp, bytes: &[u8]) -> DispatchOutcome. The C-ABI nmp-ffi::action::bytes::dispatch_action_bytes is now a thin wrapper calling dispatch_action_bytes_typed and converting to JSON. nmp-uniffi::NmpApp::dispatch_action calls dispatch_action_bytes_typed directly. The C-ABI still passes (cargo test -p nmp-ffi: all green).","tests_added":["crates/nmp-native-runtime/src/action_dispatch_tests.rs: malformed_envelope_produces_error_outcome, oversize_bytes_produce_error_outcome, dispatch_preserves_host_supplied_correlation_id, coded_rejection_carries_both_error_and_code, plain_rejection_has_error_but_no_code, unknown_namespace_produces_error_outcome","crates/nmp-uniffi/src/tests.rs: clamp_visible_zero_yields_default, clamp_visible_clamps_to_range, clamp_emit_hz_zero_yields_default, clamp_emit_hz_clamps_to_range, sink_register_and_clear, sink_replace_is_atomic, sink_panicking_callback_is_contained, clear_waits_for_in_flight_callback, shutdown_during_in_flight_update_no_uaf_no_deadlock, dispatch_malformed_envelope_produces_error_outcome, dispatch_wrapper_passes_through_correlation_id, dispatch_wrapper_passes_through_code_field"],"tests_run":["cargo test -p nmp-uniffi: 12/12 passed","cargo test -p nmp-native-runtime: 77/77 passed (71 unit + 1 integration + 5 doc-tests)","cargo test -p nmp-ffi: all passed","cargo test -p nmp-testing --test doctrine_lint_smoke: 127/127 passed"],"all_green":true,"notes":"Key implementation detail: UniFFI 0.28/0.29 generates FfiConverter impls for Box<dyn Trait> (not Arc<dyn Trait>) for callback interfaces. UpdateSink parameter in set_update_sink uses Box<dyn UpdateSink>; internally converted to Arc<dyn UpdateSink> via Arc::from(s) so the closure satisfies UpdateListener = Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync>. The shutdown() deadlock was caused by actor_starter holding the original update_tx clone: the listener thread's while let Ok(update) = update_rx.recv() loop would never exit unless both update_tx clones (actor_starter's + startup_update_tx) were dropped. Fixed by adding actor_starter.take() to shutdown(). The uniffi 'bindgen' feature was renamed to 'cli' in 0.29 for the uniffi_bindgen_main entrypoint. Cargo.toml uses version = '0.29' which resolved to 0.29.5."},"review":{"verdict":"request_changes","quiescence_sound":true,"spec_conformant":true,"findings":[{"severity":"major","issue":"crates/nmp-uniffi/src/tests.rs:222-232 `shutdown_during_in_flight_update_no_uaf_no_deadlock` does NOT create an in-flight update. It installs a non-blocking RecordSink and calls shutdown() (then again for idempotency) with no callback executing. The single highest-risk behavior the spec demanded be PROVEN — shutdown joining the listener thread WHILE a foreign on_update is mid-flight — is never exercised; the test only proves shutdown is callable and idempotent. The name overstates coverage. Fix: install a barrier-blocking sink, fire the passive pre-start snapshot so on_update is genuinely in-flight, call shutdown() on the main thread, release the barrier from a helper thread, and assert shutdown() returns (join completes) without deadlock/UAF."},{"severity":"major","issue":"crates/nmp-uniffi/src/tests.rs:170-219 `clear_waits_for_in_flight_callback` — the canonical quiescence proof — is sleep/timing-based (main sleeps 2ms then clears; worker sleeps 5ms then releases the barrier) and asserts nothing. If the listener thread processes the passive snapshot AFTER clear() sets listener=None, on_update never runs, the Barrier(2) only gets the worker's wait(), and worker.join() hangs forever (no test timeout). It also never asserts that clear() actually blocked on in_flight>0. Make it deterministic: signal callback entry via a channel/Condvar before clearing, and assert the wait happened, instead of racing on sleeps."},{"severity":"minor","issue":"crates/nmp-uniffi/src/tests.rs:148-159 `sink_panicking_callback_is_contained` does not isolate the wrapper's panic containment. The panic fires on the runtime listener thread, which already wraps the callback in its own catch_unwind (crates/nmp-native-runtime/src/app_ctor.rs:294). The test would still pass if the wrapper's catch_unwind (crates/nmp-uniffi/src/lib.rs:153) were deleted, so it does not actually guard the behavior it claims."},{"severity":"nit","issue":"Stale UniFFI version in docs: crates/nmp-uniffi/src/lib.rs:139 and crates/nmp-uniffi/src/tests.rs:14 say 'UniFFI 0.28' while Cargo.toml:37 pins uniffi = \"0.29\". The Box<dyn UpdateSink> lift type is correct for 0.29 callback_interface; only the comments are wrong and could mislead future maintainers."},{"severity":"nit","issue":"Reentrancy is documented as forbidden (crates/nmp-uniffi/src/lib.rs:57-59) but not tested. Acceptable since a true reentrancy test deadloc