91a86-f76a2 | 2026-07-03T09:18:17Z | session:91a86fdf-624c-446e-9b38-0fb02085121f | **So the clean way to get concern 3: event-source the wallet reducer.** Make current state a fold over an ordered stream of typed facts — `TokenAdded`, `TokenDeleted{cause}`, `MintProbeReconciled{proof, verdict}`, `NutzapRedeemed`, etc. — and have each fold step retain a bounded in-memory ring of "what changed + why." Then: \n - **Current state** = the fold result (concern 2), \n - **"Why is it this shape"** = replay the retained delta ring (concern 3), \n - and neither of those is your money-safety journal (concern 1), which persists separately with different correctness rules. [...] Two views over one ordered fact stream, owned by `nmp-wallet`: \n  \n ```rust \n // The fact stream — post-observation, each carrying WHY + provenance. \n enum WalletFact { \n     TokenAdded     { token_event: EventId, amount: Msat, mint: MintUrl, via: Provenance }, \n     TokenDeleted   { token_event: EventId, cause: DeleteCause },      // NIP-09 in, or local rollover \n     MintProbed     { proof: ProofRef, verdict: ProofVerdict },        // Spent / Unspent / Unknown \n     NutzapRedeemed { nutzap: EventId, amount: Msat, sender: PubkeyRef }, \n     SagaTransition { op: CorrelationId, from: OpState, to: OpState },  // producer wiring from concern 1 \n     StateRebuilt   { from: Vec<EventId> },                            // genesis fact after restart \n } [...] - **Current state** = the fold result (concern 2), \n - **"Why is it this shape"** = replay the retained delta ring (concern 3), \n - and neither of those is your money-safety journal (concern 1), which persists separately with different correctness rules. [...] The streams aren't distinguished by *lifetime* — they're distinguished by **write moment**: \n  \n - **Saga (1)** writes **pre-effect**: "about to consume proofs A,B for a mint spend." That pre-record *is* the at-most-once mechanism. Durable, money-critical. \n - **Trail (3)** writes **post-observation**: "a deletion arrived / a probe found C spent / a nutzap redeemed." Diagnostic, bounded. \n - **State (2)** is the fold over the post-observation facts. [...] The load-bearing correction: **you can't read 2/3 out of 1**, because the saga only knows *locally-initiated* operations — and most of what makes the wallet chaotic (inbound token arrivals, NIP-09 deletions from your *other* devices, incoming nutzaps) never touches the saga at all. So it's not a subset relationship. It's **producer/consumer**: the saga *emits facts into* the trail (`MintSettled`, `Unknown→reconciled`, `Failed`) so the trail can explain locally-caused shape changes too — but their schemas never merge (money-critical pre-effect records must not live in a diagnostic log with bounded eviction). [...] 1. **The reducer must be confluent** — terminal state order-*insensitive* (a delete arriving before its token must tombstone, not no-op), even though the trail is order-*sensitive*. Otherwise two devices show different balances and the trail "explains" a state that shouldn't exist.
